WEBVTT

00:00:00.073 --> 00:00:04.323
This command just got a key that a person approved.

00:00:05.095 --> 00:00:11.796
First, the machine logs in, and prints a code to enter in Dispatch.

00:00:12.553 --> 00:00:17.137
There, alice types it into the machine login page.

00:00:17.137 --> 00:00:22.420
It names example-host-build. She approves it.

00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:26.754
Back on the machine, the login is issued.

00:00:26.754 --> 00:00:31.379
Next, it registers a session for an agent.

00:00:31.379 --> 00:00:37.920
The broker calls this session an enrollment; its operator is alice.

00:00:38.123 --> 00:00:46.115
Now the session asks for the demo API key to run one command, and says why.

00:00:46.115 --> 00:00:48.617
Now it waits for a person.

00:00:48.623 --> 00:00:53.522
The request is in alice's Inbox, which links to the broker.

00:00:53.522 --> 00:00:58.172
Opening it signs her in to the broker.

00:00:58.172 --> 00:01:05.350
The broker's own page shows the session, the lifetime, and the reason.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.600
She approves it there.

00:01:07.822 --> 00:01:11.822
The waiting command gets the key, and runs.

00:01:14.035 --> 00:01:17.335
Its status says alice decided it.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:24.869
Settings lists the live grant, with alice as its approver.

00:01:24.869 --> 00:01:27.999
Each live grant has a Revoke button.
